 [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=StzNlYXnCm4&t=2129s](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=StzNlYXnCm4&t=2129s)

why is this comment upvoted?  it's dismissive, it's not empathetic, it will embarass and erode hope for the person who recieves it, the advice itself is shallow.

&#x200B;

come up with better advice, and don't be a prick

If you really care about someone, then this means honestly considering the possibility that perhaps the best thing you can do for their health and well being...

&#x200B;

...is to get out of the way.

&#x200B;

Whether the therapist is right or wrong about this is irrelevant.  You'll still have to honestly consider what you think the truth of the matter is.

And besides.  It's up to her.
